The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.

NOTES:
- The cylinder?a and cylinder? examples are in the b-tensor formulation,
  whereas the cylinder_c? examples are in the c-tensor formulation,
  (standard c or logc).
- Examples having a _mm added to the name are extended from the problem
  without the _mm added. The problems use a multi-mode EGP model
  with the option to use a global von Mises stress.
- Examples having a _gammap added to the name are extended from the problem
  without the _gammap added. The problems use an EGP model with plastic strain 
  softening. In case of explicit time integration an additional problem for
  the equivalent plastic strain is introduced:
    Problem 3: Equivalent plastic strain (gammap)
- The examples are modified versions of the examples with the same filename
  in confined_cylinder_b. Hence, by taking a diff, it is easy to find the
  difference and adapt your own problem to the EGP model.
- For more creating more refined meshes, see the corresponding subdirectory
  meshes in the example directory confined_cylinder_b.

Short description
-----------------

cylinder1a, cylinder1a_mm, cylinder1a_mm_gammap

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for an incompressible EGP model using
 the b-tensor formulation. Explicit div tau term.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-explicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: b tensor

cylinder3a

 (This problem is similar to cylinder1a, but solved using fully-implicit
  with Newton-Raphson for the b-tensor equation).

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for an incompressible EGP model using
 the b-tensor formulation. Explicit div tau term.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson for the b-tensor.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-explicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: b tensor

cylinder6a

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation of an incompressible
 EGP model.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally exclude certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder7

 (This problem is similar to cylinder6a, but now with a final steady state step)

 Startup + steady state of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation of
 an incompressible EGP model.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson.
 After the final time step do a iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder8, cylinder8_mm

 Sequence of steady states of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation of
 an incompressible EGP model.
 Iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson.
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder9

 (This problem is similar to cylinder1a_mm, but now with two subprocesses in the
  multi-moded EGP model. Each subprocess defines its own von-Mises stress.)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for an incompressible EGP model using
 the b-tensor formulation. Explicit div tau term.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-explicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: b tensor
 Multi-mode/multi-process EGP model with two subprocesses. Each subprocess
 defines its own von-Mises stress.

cylinder10

 (This problem is similar to cylinder8_mm, but now with two subprocesses in the
  multi-moded EGP model. Each subprocess defines its own von-Mises stress.)

 Sequence of steady states of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation of
 an incompressible EGP model.
 Iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson.
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.
 Multi-mode/multi-process EGP model with two subprocesses. Each subprocess
 defines its own von-Mises stress.


cylinder_c1, cylinder_c1_mm

 (This problem is similar to cylinder1a, but solved using c/logc)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for an incompressible EGP model using
 the conformation tensor formulation. Explicit div tau term.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-explicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: Conformation tensor

cylinder_c3

 (This problem is similar to cylinder3a, but solved using the c-tensor)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for an incompressible EGP model using
 the conformation tensor formulation. Explicit div tau term.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson for the conformation tensor.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-explicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: Conformation tensor

cylinder_c6

 (This problem is similar to cylinder6a, but solved using the c-tensor)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for an incompressible EGP model using
 the conformation tensor formulation.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally exclude certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder_c7

 (This problem is similar to cylinder_c6, but now with a final steady state
  step)

 Startup + steady state of flow around a cylinder for an incompressible EGP
 model using the conformation tensor formulation.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson.
 After the final time step do a iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder_c8

 (This problem is similar to cylinder8, but solved using the c-tensor)

 Sequence of steady states of flow around a cylinder for an incompressible EGP
 model using the conformation tensor formulation.
 Iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson.
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder_c9

 (This problem is similar to cylinder_c1_mm, but now with two subprocesses in
  the multi-moded EGP model. Each subprocess defines its own von-Mises stress.)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for an incompressible EGP model using
 the conformation tensor formulation. Explicit div tau term.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-explicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: Conformation tensor
 Multi-mode/multi-process EGP model with two subprocesses. Each subprocess
 defines its own von-Mises stress.

